{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThree external-test modules contain repeated, historical, decorative, or obvious prose. Their contents are unchanged from the audit and revalidated on `origin/main` at `0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e`.\n\n## Approach\nCondense only the listed blocks. Preserve non-docstring AST, runtime fixture data, sentinels, markers, assertions, and exact directives. Keep live-test intent complete without duplicating assertions or helper-owned logic.\n\n## Scope\n- `test_structured_output_matrix.py:1-22,49-53,114-120,139-144,193` — Preserve live-call-only scope; exact provider × directive × production-prompt × repeat matrix; raw artifacts; helper ownership of deterministic scoring/credentials/budgets; the agentic first-object trap plus single-shot control; one unparsed text-mode call; and partial-run/all-skip semantics. Delete the obvious score-table narration at 193.\n- `test_verified_fake_contract_live.py:1-18` — Preserve shared-contract/real-client purpose, fixture-recapture drift signal, opt-in requirements, and separate authenticated-`acli` requirement for search.\n- `test_workflow_live.py:1-15,37-39,69,91-98,110-111,115` — Preserve real `RunnerAgentStep`, `review_skeleton` stage path, live prompt resolution, provider routing, terminal-step contract, and the guarantee that missing `{{plan}}` in verify/coach does not degrade to `INDETERMINATE`; delete comments already made obvious by assertions/docstrings.\n\nRetain out-of-scope sentinel, production-spacing, budget, provider-selection, stable-key, non-vacuity, replay, security-overlay, schema, and fixture-data comments. Consumers include structured-output and external-integration workflows, external conftest gates/fixtures, shared Jira-shape contracts, hermetic counterparts, documented live checks, provider/scorer tests, and live-reachability guards. No autodoc/`__doc__` consumer exists. Preserve the `import rebar  # noqa: F401` directive exactly.\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The leaf commit changes only comments/true docstrings or blank lines in the declared, reviewed blocks; non-docstring AST, runtime strings, assertions, and exact directives remain unchanged.\n- [ ] A reviewer who did not author the remediation posts a leaf-linked TSV with one row per edited block: path/block, pinned before citation, final-commit after citation (or DELETED plus neighbor), preserved contract/consumer, before/after words, semantic-preservation verdict, bloat-removal verdict, and reviewer session.\n- [ ] Every row has `semantic-preservation=PASS` and `bloat-removal=PASS`; bloat removal requires shorter text with repetition/history/ornament removed rather than relocated.\n- [ ] Recorded focused checks, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify` pass.\n- [ ] Missing or FAIL rows block closure.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded normalized AST/directive guard, focused tests, diff check, and `make verify`. The independent TSV judges prose quality."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788611719704018001,"uuid":"54f8b135-fff7-4125-a480-5f902c105726"}